## 2. Fork Identification

Any distributed version of the Software that has been modified from the
original version must clearly and prominently identify itself as a fork,
modified version, or derivative work of the original Software.

The identification must make clear that the modified version is not the
official version of the original Software.

Acceptable examples include:

* "Fork of GO Live"
* "Modified version of Go Live"
* "Based on Go Live"
* "Unofficial fork of Go Live"

The identification must not be removed, hidden, or presented in a manner
reasonably likely to cause users to believe that the modified version is the
official version of the original Software.

## 3. Preservation of Copyright and License Notices

The copyright notice, this license, and existing attribution notices included
with the original Software must be preserved in copies and substantial
portions of the Software.

## 4. Source Code

When distributing modified versions of the Software, the distributor must
make the corresponding source code available under the terms of this license.

